-- title:
--   Deligne's integral representation over the canonical coefficient completion
-- statement:
--   Let $N>0$, let $k\ge2$, let $p$ be prime, and let $f$ be a normalized algebraic cuspidal Hecke eigenform of level $N$, weight $k$ and nebentype $\varepsilon_f$. Fix an embedding of the algebraic numbers into $\mathbb C_p$. Let $K_f$ be the field generated by all Fourier coefficients and nebentype values, let $\mathfrak p_f$ be the prime selected by the embedding, and put
--
--   $$R=\varprojlim_n\mathcal O_{K_f}/\mathfrak p_f^n.$$
--
--   There exists a representation on an integral lattice with a chosen basis,
--
--   $$\rho:G_{\mathbb Q}\longrightarrow\operatorname{GL}_2(R),$$
--
--   such that every reduction modulo $\mathfrak p_f^n$ factors through a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, inertia acts trivially outside $Np$, and at each prime $\ell\nmid Np$ every arithmetic Frobenius lift satisfies
--
--   $$\operatorname{tr}\rho(\operatorname{Frob}_\ell)=a_\ell(f),\qquad
--   \det\rho(\operatorname{Frob}_\ell)=\varepsilon_f(\ell)\ell^{k-1}.$$
--
--   The values on the right are mapped from $\mathcal O_{K_f}$ into $R$. The formal statement uses a monoid homomorphism into matrices; its values are automatically invertible because its source is a group. Congruence continuity is expressed at every ideal power by `GaloisFactorsThroughFiniteLevel`. The inertia and Frobenius conditions use valuation subrings of the actual algebraic closure, with residue Frobenius $x\mapsto x^\ell$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-zero Deligne theorem on a stable integral lattice. Deligne–Serre Theorem 6.1 supplies the representation over $(K_f)_{\mathfrak p_f}$ for any eigenform of weight at least two; it does not require newness or a trivial nebentype. Its compact image preserves an integral lattice (§6.12). The ring of integers of this local field identifies with the displayed adic completion; choosing a basis gives the stated form. The finite-level congruence assertions follow from continuity.
--
--   This theorem is the remaining deep input for reducing to the mission's residual representation. It asserts a full integral representation in characteristic zero, rather than assuming the existence of the requested residual kernel field.
-- source:
--   Deligne–Serre, Formes modulaires de poids 1, Ann. Sci. ENS 7 (1974), Theorem 6.1, p.520 (all weights at least two, arbitrary nebentype and any coefficient number field containing the eigenvalues), and §6.12, p.523 (stable integral lattice and reduction). Arithmetic Frobenius convention: footnote on p.513. https://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/Number24.pdf. The integral representation and its residual reduction are used in Kriz–Nordentoft, arXiv:2310.20678v3, §4, equation (4.2).

import Definitions.Def_KN_EigenformResidualGaloisRepresentationV2
import Definitions.Def_MTT_EigenformCoefficientCompletion
import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_Residual

set_option autoImplicit false
noncomputable section

open NumberField

/-- Deligne's representation on a stable integral lattice at the chosen coefficient prime. -/
theorem MTT.Eigenform.exists_adic_matrix_representation
    {N k p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] (hN : 0 < N) (hk : 2 ≤ k)
    (ι : MTT.Qbar →+* ℂ) (f : MTT.Eigenform N k ι)
    (ιp : MTT.Qbar →+* ℂ_[p]) :
    ∃ ρ : (MTT.Qbar ≃ₐ[ℚ] MTT.Qbar) →*
        Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) (f.coefficientCompletion ιp),
      (∀ n : ℕ, GaloisFactorsThroughFiniteLevel
        (((AdicCompletion.evalₐ (f.coefficientPrime ιp) n).toRingHom.mapMatrix
          (m := Fin 2)).toMonoidHom.comp ρ)) ∧
      (∀ (l : ℕ), l.Prime → Nat.Coprime l (N * p) →
        ∀ A : ValuationSubring MTT.Qbar, A.LiesOverPrime l →
          ∀ σ ∈ A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ, ρ σ = 1) ∧
      (∀ (l : ℕ), l.Prime → Nat.Coprime l (N * p) →
        ∀ A : ValuationSubring MTT.Qbar, A.LiesOverPrime l →
          ∀ σ : MTT.Qbar ≃ₐ[ℚ] MTT.Qbar, A.IsFrobeniusAt σ l →
            Matrix.trace (ρ σ) =
              algebraMap (𝓞 f.coefficientField) (f.coefficientCompletion ιp)
                (f.integralCoeff hN hk l) ∧
            Matrix.det (ρ σ) =
              algebraMap (𝓞 f.coefficientField) (f.coefficientCompletion ιp)
                (f.integralNebentype (l : ZMod N) *
                  (l : 𝓞 f.coefficientField) ^ (k - 1))) := by
  sorry
